---
title: "Drawbridge — J1: a Tier-1 vendor review, intake to approval"
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor M as Marcus · Procurement
  participant D as Dashboard
  participant O as Orchestrator
  participant PS as Pub/Sub
  participant Q as Questionnaire
  actor V as Vendor contact
  participant A as Ingress · Model Armor
  participant E as Evidence
  participant R as Risk Scorer
  actor EL as Elena · CISO

  rect rgb(219, 234, 254)
  Note over M,O: Day 0 — intake and planning, minutes not weeks
  M->>D: Submit NimbusWrite AI, processes customer text, 40k per year
  D->>PS: publish review.intake
  PS->>O: deliver intake event
  O->>O: recall dossier from Memory Bank, tier the vendor
  Note right of O: Tier 1 — processes customer data<br/>and is an AI service. When ambiguous, tier up.
  O->>PS: publish review.plan_ready with checkpointed plan
  end

  rect rgb(255, 237, 213)
  Note over Q,V: Day 0 — the fleet asks permission before it speaks to an outsider
  PS->>Q: deliver plan_ready
  Q->>Q: select and tailor 60 questions from the bank
  Q--xD: gateway blocks send — P1 requires an approval token
  D->>M: approval card — the review parks at the P1 gate, scope contact
  M->>D: one tap authorises first contact
  D->>Q: signed single-use token, scope email
  Q->>V: questionnaire, under idempotency key questionnaire_send v1
  end

  rect rgb(220, 252, 231)
  Note over V,E: Days 1 and 2 — replies arrive in fragments, evidence is screened
  V->>A: partial replies and a SOC 2 report
  A->>A: extract locally, scrub PII, screen for injection
  A->>PS: publish evidence.screened with clean-stamp
  PS->>Q: deliver reply events
  Q->>Q: parse incrementally, merge by question id, record confidence
  Q->>V: chase round 2 on schedule, its own idempotency key chase round2
  PS->>E: deliver screened evidence
  E->>E: pass 1 Flash — extract control claims
  E->>E: pass 2 Pro — reconcile claims against answers
  E->>PS: findings ready, MFA claim contradicts SOC 2 exception, severity high
  end

  rect rgb(243, 232, 255)
  Note over R,EL: Day 3 — scoring and the human gate
  PS->>R: deliver findings_ready
  R->>R: deterministic rubric arithmetic in Python, not in the prompt
  R->>R: one Pro call writes the CISO memo
  R->>D: score 71, band conditional, memo and score breakdown
  D->>EL: gate card with findings and reasoning
  EL->>D: approve with conditions, identity and timestamp recorded
  D->>PS: publish review.approved
  PS->>O: close the review, write the dossier to Memory Bank
  O->>D: audit binder available for export
  end

  Note over M,EL: Three weeks of calendar review compressed to about three days, and roughly<br/>fifty analyst hours to under one. Vendor reply latency is the floor — the fleet adds none of its own.
